# Docker build context is the repo root (see infra ApiServiceConstruct: directory="."), but the
# Dockerfile only COPYs src/api + src/__init__.py. Without this file Docker ships the ENTIRE repo
# to the daemon as build context on every synth/deploy — including cdk.out (tens of GB), .venv,
# node_modules, and .git — which is the dominant cause of slow `npx projen deploy`. Exclude
# everything the image doesn't need so the context is tiny and cache-stable.

# CDK synth output — huge (bundled assets, templates); never needed in an image.
cdk.out/

# Python virtualenv + caches.
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Node / frontend — the console is built separately (build:console) and served from S3, not
# from this container.
**/node_modules/
src/console/dist/
src/console/

# VCS + IDE + agent tooling. Agent skills and issue worktrees are development inputs, never API
# runtime inputs; excluding them also prevents an accidentally nested worktree from inflating
# every staged CDK Docker asset.
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
.agents/
.claude/
.kiro/

# Docs, tests, plans, review artifacts — not part of the API runtime.
docs/
tests/
ai-review-*
report.xml

# Local settings / secrets (belt-and-suspenders; also gitignored).
settings.py

# Local scratch files that are not tracked but ARE in the build context, so they shift the API
# image's asset fingerprint (issue #50). Screenshots, OS metadata and one-off dev scripts are never
# API runtime inputs; excluding them keeps the hash a function of the SOURCE, not of whatever
# happens to be lying in the working tree.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
scripts/dev/

# Coverage data, and NOT only for hash stability — leaving it out was breaking CI. pytest-xdist
# workers write `.coverage.<host>.<pid>.<rand>` into the repo root, which is this build context, and
# a test that synths the stack makes jsii walk and hash the root. It listed a worker's temp file and
# then tried to open it after the worker exited and deleted it:
#   RuntimeError: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.coverage.runner-…pid851.XJpCeQzx'
# The failing test was unrelated to whatever change was under review, which is the expensive part —
# it reads as "your branch broke an acceptance test". The hash argument applies too: with these
# present the API image's fingerprint depends on which workers happened to still be running.
.coverage
.coverage.*

# CI-only caches that live INSIDE the build context (GitLab requires cache paths under
# $CI_PROJECT_DIR). Every stack-synthesizing test makes CDK walk and hash this root, so leaving
# these in cost ~100-155s PER TEST in CI for tests that run in 0.7s locally. See .gitlab-ci.yml:
# UV_CACHE_DIR and JSII_RUNTIME_PACKAGE_CACHE_ROOT.
.uv_cache/
.jsii_cache/
